# Generated artifacts must keep their exact bytes.
#
# Every rule here protects something that is CHECKED against recorded bytes, so a
# checkout that rewrites line endings would fail a test for a reason that has
# nothing to do with what the test is about.

# The TipTap bundle (PH1-10). Its size is recorded in the esbuild metafile next to
# it, and test_tiptap_bundle.py compares the two -- so a CRLF conversion on
# checkout would break a provenance check for purely mechanical reasons. It is also
# a build output, not source to be normalised.
erpnext_construction_ph/erpnext_construction_ph/public/js/editor/tiptap.bundle.js -text

# The same build's inputs and record: the bundle entry (bare specifiers, never
# served) and the metafile (a record of one specific build). A spurious diff on a
# regenerated metafile trains people to ignore the file that carries provenance.
erpnext_construction_ph/erpnext_construction_ph/tools/* -text

# The vendored BCF schemas are byte-pinned by SHA-256 against upstream
# (test_vendored_schemas_are_byte_identical_to_upstream), and CC BY-ND forbids
# editing them at all. A checkout that rewrote them would fail a provenance test
# for a reason that has nothing to do with provenance.
erpnext_construction_ph/erpnext_construction_ph/construction_ph/bcf/schema/** -text
